  ],
  "description": "BBE 482i, engaged channel B. Audio board parts and NJM2153 filter topology follow Tom Farrand’s 8 September 2004 Rev. 0 analysis. Gain behavior is referenced to the New Japan Radio NJM2153 data sheet. The two integrators feed the high, mid and low paths of the summing amplifier. Process changes high-band level, Lo Contour changes low-band level, and the mid path is fixed. The proprietary peak detector and high-band VCA use a functional fit with a 0.235–1 gain range, 22 µF/3.32 kΩ release and a 4.7 Ω charge resistance. TL072 sections approximate the chip amplifiers. LED meters and bypass are omitted.",
  "groundNode": "0",
  "inputNode": "in",
  "layout": {
    "pots": [
      "Lo Contour",
      "Process"
    ]
  },
  "name": "BBE 482i Sonic Maximizer Channel B",
  "outputNode": "out",
  "version": 3,
